g.yml from user-service-config (rw,path="jaeger-config.yml")\n      /social-network-microservices/config/service-config.json from user-service-config (rw,path="service-config.json")\n      /user-service-data from user-service-volume (rw)\n  Volumes:\n   user-service-config:\n    Type:      ConfigMap (a volume populated by a ConfigMap)\n    Name:      user-service\n    Optional:  false\n   user-service-volume:\n    Type:          PersistentVolumeClaim (a reference to a PersistentVolumeClaim in the same namespace)\n    ClaimName:     temp-pvc\n    ReadOnly:      false\n  Node-Selectors:  kubernetes.io/hostname=node2.htliang2-agent.insai-pg0.apt.emulab.net\n  Tolerations:     <none>\nConditions:\n  Type           Status  Reason\n  ----           ------  ------\n  Available      False   MinimumReplicasUnavailable\n  Progressing    True    ReplicaSetUpdated\nOldReplicaSets:  <none>\nNewReplicaSet:   user-service-cdd678d87 (1/1 replicas created)\nEvents:\n  Type    Reason             Age   From                   Message\n  ----    ------             ----  ----                   -------\n  Normal  ScalingReplicaSet  41s   deployment-controller  Scaled up replica set user-service-cdd678d87 to 1\n', id='de0f555a-6672-4b56-ae30-b77884936925', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-b578ff0defa50b8a'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='b7b1a719-baac-44dd-9c29-35db54b63090'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user-service deployment is not available, with 0 pods ready. The previous step showed that the deployment is trying to create a pod, but it\'s not succeeding. The event mentions "MinimumReplicasUnavailable," which usually means the replicas aren\'t meeting the desired state.\n\nFirst, I should check the pods associated with this deployment. The command "kubectl get pods -n social-network" was run earlier, and user-service was listed a