node selector pointing to node2. Maybe that node is down or not available. I should check the node\'s status. Also, looking at the events, the deployment scaled up the replica set, but the pod might not be running. Let me check the pod\'s describe output to see why it\'s not starting. \n\nAnother angle: the container might be failing to start. Using "kubectl describe pod" on the user-service pod would show logs, events, and reasons for failure. If the pod is in Pending state, maybe the node selector is incorrect, or there\'s no available node. If it\'s in CrashLoopBackOff, there\'s an application error. Also, checking the logs with "kubectl logs" could reveal specific errors. \n\nSince the user-service is the only one with 0/1, focusing on that pod is crucial. Let me run "kubectl describe pod" for the user-service pod to get more details on why it\'s not available. That should help identify the root cause, like image issues, resource limits, or configuration errors.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \n"kubectl describe pod -n social-network"  \nTo investigate the specific status and events of the user-service pod (which is in a 0/1 state), I need to examine its detailed logs, events, and container status. This will reveal whether the pod is crashing, pending, or failing due to resource constraints, image issues, or configuration errors. This step is critical to pinpoint the exact cause of the deployment failure.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 470, 'prompt_tokens': 3145, 'total_tokens': 3615, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfcc0-50ae-74f0-8bb3-caef56f56852-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3145, 'output_tokens': 470, 'total_tokens': 3615}), HumanM